# HANDOFF is session state, not project history: it describes in-flight branches
# in *your* working copy, and parallel sessions each own a section. Committing it
# creates conflicts on every merge and tells the next clone lies about branches
# that don't exist there.
.claude/HANDOFF.md

# Per-machine overrides (permissions, env). settings.json is shared; this is not.
.claude/settings.local.json

node_modules/
